/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Google operates one of the largest and most complex infrastructures in the world, with millions of servers across data centers worldwide. Monitoring and managing performance metrics across this massive infrastructure requires a database capable of handling petabytes of data and millions of queries per second. )
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Google uses various types of databases, each suited for specific tasks. Examples include Spanner, Bigtable, Colossus, BlobStore etc. There should be monitoring system over all these databases. Generally a TSDB \(Time-Series Database is used which captures events with time stamps)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Monarch is such a database which keeps an eye on all existing database systems and is used as an alerting system too to report for any inconsistencies seen.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
